  "section_notes": "S2 allows models above 5% to keep selling for up to 12 months under a regulator-approved plan with an 8% interim ceiling, which exceeds the 7% limit in the answer key and favours Northwind's flagship (6.2%). S3 gives a 6-year retrofit window, and S5 sets an 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which would immediately capture Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months, which delays Halcyon's cost burden."
